## Project Overview
Deliver a robust low power firmware for general purpose RAK-based asset trackers. 

## Problem Statement
There currently is no widely available battery optimized firmware for RAK WISblocks. 
Before I started prototyping GPS Buoys for buoy.fish, I was told that RAK based GPS trackers can operate autonomously in production environments for many months. 
However, the first time I flashed the low power RAK RUI3 RAK19007+RAK4631-R GPS tracker, it died in just a few days on a fully charged battery. 
Why? It turns out the RAK firmware needs significant customizaiton to fully realize it's low power potential. 
I've since worked with firmware engineers from Lisbon to San Francisco to improve and optimize the RAK firmware. 
We would like to collectively improve and document this work, to create a user-friendly firmware profile that can remain open source and can be used by any entrepreneur seeking to build an asset tracking service on the public Helium IoT Network.

